WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
One of the one of the questions

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.535
that I've had throughout

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.205
this classified documents case is why?

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.906
Why did he do this?

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.641
And I've asked a lot of people who know

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.644
Donald Trump well why they think it is.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.614
You obviously know Donald Trump well.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.016
Here is a couple

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.783
here are a couple of theories

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.052
I asked of former Secretary of defense

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.587
under Trump. Mark Esper.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.189
I want to get your reaction to this.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.125
I I've heard two different theories

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.726
as to why he had these documents.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.596
One from Stephanie Grisham, who said

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.131
he just like,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:31.364
you know,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.032
these are mine

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.566
and he's like a child with a toy

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.567
And one from Michael Cohen.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.769
He said he thought that

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.770
Trump had these documents

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.705
because he wanted to use them

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:42.075
to further his own power or financial

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.376
well-being in some way.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.811
Why do you think he held on

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:45.478
to these documents

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.480
and went to such lengths

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.715
to stop them,

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.616
to prevent them from being

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.650
turned over to the government

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.686
Yeah, look, I think both

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.521
theories can be true

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.823
and like they are true to some extent.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.357
I have to admit,

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.191
I was kind of surprised

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.359
that Esper said that

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.160
because the idea

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.261
that he would use these secrets

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.228
to further his own power,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.029
financial well-being,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.898
is a shocking thing for him to think.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:05.899
What do you think?

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.934
I think it was purely ego.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.436
I think, Jake, he could not

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:10.603
and still cannot to this day

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.671
deal with the fact

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:11.938
that he's

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.872
the only person outside

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:13.573
the state of Delaware

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.208
to ever lose to Joe Biden.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.443
And he wants to pretend

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.744
he's still president.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.145
He takes these boxes with him

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.246
like he flies

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.314
them up there in New Jersey.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.549
Now, if he still had them,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.249
they'd be in New Jersey

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.150
because they go on

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.919
summer vacation with him.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.519
I mean,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.620
he wanted to continue

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.322
to pretend he was president

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.990
and show these things to people

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.558
and say, look,

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.626
I still have work with I still know.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.761
So it's all part of the kabuki

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.762
about people telling him,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.030
oh, you're still president.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.331
You actually won that whole.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.467
Yes, absolutely. I think that's it.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.734
And I will tell you that

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.203
I've seen him with it's

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:43.870
not the first time

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.506
also with boxes of documents in 2016

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.241
when I was campaigning with him,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.609
his bodyguard at the time,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.145
he sure would have a box of bankers,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.680
box of documents

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.814
that would go everywhere with him

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.915
when he was campaigning.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.183
And whenever he got on the plane,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.551
he would put that box of chocolates

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.687
right next to Donald Trump on the plane.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.321
He would open them.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.522
Now those documents for Trump

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.857
were from Trump Tower

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:04.524
and were business

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.692
related and also newspaper

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.559
articles, whatever.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.093
And he,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.561
he wanted that box

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.663
next to him immediately.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.731
Before we took off.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.966
So the talk about

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.868
the Beautiful Mind documents

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.269
that the staff is talking about,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.804
he was obsessed about it.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.172
There's an element to that as well.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:19.973
And I thought

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.541
going all the way back to 20, 16.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.642
I want to ask you about

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.877
what's happening in Ukraine right now,

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:24.477
because you're running

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.712
to be commander in chief, obviously.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.613
And your fellow

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.480
Republican contender

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.481
Mike Pence said on the Hugh

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.382
Hewitt Show yesterday

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.017
that if Ukraine is defeated in the war,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.518
the U.S.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.252
will ultimately,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.019
he fears,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.021
have to send troops to fight

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.456
Russia's further aggression.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.158
He seemed to be suggesting that

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.160
Russia would go and the U.S.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:40.860
would need to defend

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.061
fellow NATO's allies,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.229
which is required by charter.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.696
Do you agree?

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:45.331
Look, I

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.366
don't think

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.368
I don't think that's necessarily true.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.435
But what I do

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.403
think is

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.371
that this has huge

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.506
geopolitical implications, Jake.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.208
We have to make sure

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.809
that we send a very clear message

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.011
not only to Russia,

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.279
but quite frankly,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.513
they're my third concern

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.415
in this trifecta.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.350
China and Iran,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.185
China and Iran

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.252
are both actively

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.820
supporting Russia in this effort

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.023
with both military hardware and cash

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.091
to support Russia's effort in use.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.560
Iranian drones, for example,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.128
Iranian drones are killing civilians

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.263
every week in Ukraine.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.166
And if we do not stand with Ukraine

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.869
and help them to win this war,

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.270
the message that it sends to Iran

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.572
is they can do whatever they want to do

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.573
in the Middle East,

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.074
including vis-a-vis Israel.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:28.875
It will change the way

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.211
Saudi Arabia has to conduct itself

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:31.744
in the Middle East

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.513
because of freeing Iran up

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.480
to do these things.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.782
And China will be looking

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.684
voraciously at Taiwan

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.019
This is already a proxy war

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.821
with China and Iran.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.489
We have to win that proxy war.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.390
Quite frankly,

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.492
Russia's my third concern in all this.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.160
Very interesting.

